1. JavaScript Basics

    Data Types: Understanding primitive (String, Number, Boolean, Null, Undefined, Symbol) and non-primitive (Objects, Arrays).
    Variables & Scope: var, let, const, hoisting, and variable shadowing.
    Operators: Arithmetic, Comparison, Logical, Assignment, and Ternary operators.
    Type Conversion: Implicit and explicit conversions, and understanding == vs ===.

2. Control Structures

    Conditional Statements: if, else, else if, and switch.
    Loops: for, while, do...while, and the for...of and for...in loops.
    Error Handling: try, catch, finally, and throw.

3. Functions and Scope

    Function Declarations vs Expressions
    Arrow Functions and this behavior.
    Higher-Order Functions: Functions that take other functions as arguments or return them (e.g., map, filter, reduce).
    Closures: Scope chaining and understanding lexical scoping.
    Callback Functions: Asynchronous programming using callbacks.

4. Advanced Function Concepts

    IIFE (Immediately Invoked Function Expressions)
    Currying and Partial Application
    Memoization for optimization.
    Debouncing and Throttling for optimizing event handlers in the DOM.

5. Asynchronous JavaScript

    Promises: Understanding .then(), .catch(), .finally().
    Async/Await: Writing asynchronous code with async/await syntax.
    Event Loop & Call Stack: How JavaScript handles asynchronous code execution.
    Fetch API and AJAX: Making HTTP requests using fetch and XMLHttpRequest.
    Error Handling in Async Code

6. Data Structures and Algorithms in JavaScript

    Arrays: Built-in methods like push, pop, shift, unshift, map, filter, reduce, find, sort, every, some, includes.
    Objects: Creation, manipulation, Object.keys(), Object.values(), Object.entries(), Object.assign().
    Sets and Maps: Unique collections with fast lookups.
    Strings: Methods like split, slice, substr, replace, toUpperCase, toLowerCase, includes, and regular expressions.
    Algorithms: Sorting, searching, and traversing through arrays and objects.

7. Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)

    Prototypes and Inheritance: Prototype chain, prototype inheritance, and Object.create.
    Classes and Constructors: ES6 classes, constructors, and methods.
    Encapsulation, Abstraction, Inheritance, and Polymorphism: Core OOP principles.
    this Keyword: How this behaves in different contexts (global, object methods, arrow functions).

8. JavaScript Design Patterns

    Module Pattern: Encapsulating code.
    Singleton Pattern: Ensuring a class has only one instance.
    Factory Pattern: Creating objects with shared properties or methods.
    Observer Pattern: Event handling in JavaScript.

9. Document Object Model (DOM) Manipulation

    Selecting Elements: Using getElementById, getElementsByClassName, querySelector, and querySelectorAll.
    Modifying Elements: Changing text, attributes, classes, and styles dynamically.
    Event Handling: Attaching events with addEventListener, event delegation, and removing event listeners.
    DOM Traversal: Navigating through elements (parentNode, childNodes, nextSibling, etc.).

10. Browser APIs

    Local Storage and Session Storage: Storing data in the browser.
    Cookies: Setting, getting, and managing cookies.
    Web APIs: Geolocation, Notification, WebSockets, and File API.
    Timers: Using setTimeout and setInterval for delayed or repeated execution.

11. ES6+ Features

    Arrow Functions and concise syntax.
    Destructuring: For arrays and objects.
    Spread and Rest Operators: Working with arrays and objects.
    Template Literals: Embedding expressions within strings.
    Modules: import and export for modular code.
    Default, Rest, and Spread Syntax

12. Event-Driven Programming

    Event Propagation: Bubbling, capturing, and stopping propagation.
    Custom Events: Creating and dispatching custom events.
    Event Delegation: Managing events efficiently by delegating to parent elements.

13. Memory Management and Optimization

    Memory Leaks: Identifying and avoiding memory leaks.
    Garbage Collection: How JavaScript manages memory.
    Performance Optimization: Tips for reducing computational and memory overhead.

14. Testing and Debugging

    Debugging in Console: console.log, console.error, console.warn, console.table.
    Breakpoints and Watch Expressions: Using Developer Tools.
    Unit Testing with Jest or Mocha/Chai
    Common Debugging Patterns

15. Miscellaneous and Best Practices

    Coding Standards and Best Practices: Code readability, commenting, modularity.
    Immutable vs Mutable Objects: Understanding and handling immutability.
    Designing APIs and Writing Clean Code
    Security in JavaScript: Common vulnerabilities like XSS, CSRF, and security best practices.
    Big O Notation: Understanding time and space complexity.

